          "canonical_content_sha256": "6b077431bc6cbf1fcc18b9e95aa8a59366004d23c99f4334829f3616ce32ba33",
          "canonical_content_text": "Meta's Muse AI agent achieves strong growth, company introduces new shares to power investments\n\nMeta will issue a new class of non-voting Class C common stock in January ​2027, effectively resulting in a two-for-one split, to fund acquisitions and retain top talent while maintaining CEO Mark Zuckerberg's control amid Silicon Valley's intensifying AI ​race.\n\nThe company raised the lower end of its annual spending forecast, now expecting capital expenditure to be between $135 billion and $145 billion this year, up from $130 billion to $145 billion expected previously.\n\nThe company reported better-than-expected revenue of $64.60 billion for the quarter ended September 30, ahead of Wall Street estimates of $63.37 billion, according to data compiled by LSEG.\n\nMeta reported a free cash flow deficit of $2.12 billion in the third quarter, compared with positive free cash ​flow of $10.63 billion a year earlier.",
